agent-vm is built from, and its release binaries contain, the following
projects. Their licenses and notices are in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES, and
`agent-vm licenses` prints them.

  Lima              https://github.com/lima-vm/lima                   Apache-2.0
  sshocker          https://github.com/lima-vm/sshocker               Apache-2.0
  gvisor-tap-vsock  https://github.com/containers/gvisor-tap-vsock    Apache-2.0
  pkg/sftp          https://github.com/pkg/sftp                       BSD-2-Clause

The third_party/ folder holds each of these as its upstream source at the
commit recorded in third_party/SOURCES, with the patches in patches/ applied
and nothing else (scripts/third-party-sync rebuilds it, and CI checks it).

Modifications, as section 4(b) of the Apache License 2.0 requires: the files
of Lima, sshocker and gvisor-tap-vsock that the patches in patches/lima,
patches/sshocker and patches/gvisor-tap-vsock change have been modified by
agent-vm. The patches are the complete statement of the changes; their
purpose is described in patches/README.md. pkg/sftp is modified the same way
(patches/sftp), under its BSD-2-Clause license.

The NOTICE of Lima is reproduced in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES, as section 4(d) of
the Apache License 2.0 asks.
